---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="agents"
  title="A daemon owns the processes, so an agent's shell can end and nothing dies."
  more={{ href: '/agents/', label: 'More about agents' }}
>
  <p>
    An agent can start a stack for its changes and give you a localhost URL to test. It uses the
    same commands you use to inspect logs or stop services, and the daemon keeps those services
    running when the agent's session ends.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Claude Code and Codex plugin teaches the agent the CLI and refuses a dev server started in
    the background, where nothing supervises it and its logs are lost.
  </p>
  <Terminal slot="visual" title="agent session">
    <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="dim">agent&gt;</span> pnpm dev &amp;
<span class="failure">Blocked by the devlanes plugin:</span> this starts a long-running process in the background, where nothing supervises it and its logs are lost.
Use instead:
  devlanes start [UNIT...]               services defined in devlanes.yaml
  devlanes exec --name NAME -- COMMAND   any other long-running command
Then check it with `devlanes wait NAME --timeout 180s` and `devlanes logs NAME --tail 100`.

<span class="dim">agent&gt;</span> devlanes start
myapp@3 (agent/perf): 3/3 ready
<span class="success">ready</span> api    http://127.0.0.1:20030  <span class="url">https://api.myapp3.localhost</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> web    http://127.0.0.1:20031  <span class="url">https://myapp3.localhost</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> worker http://127.0.0.1:20032</pre>
  </Terminal>
</Section>
